  "content": {
    "id": "p14-g11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Factorise the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-g11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^3-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x^2+x+1)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1^3-1\\\\P(1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x-1$ is a factor. By long division,\n$$\\begin{array}{r|l}&x^2+x+1\\\\\\hline x-1&x^3+0x^2+0x-1\\\\&-(x^3-x^2)\\\\\\hline &x^2+0x-1\\\\&-(x^2-x)\\\\\\hline &x-1\\\\&-(x-1)\\\\\\hline &0\\end{array}$$\n$$P(x)=(x-1)(x^2+x+1).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 116
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-g11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^3+8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+2)(x^2-2x+4)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3+8$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-2)&=(-2)^3+8\\\\P(-2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x+2$ is a factor. By long division,\n$$\\begin{array}{r|l}&x^2-2x+4\\\\\\hline x+2&x^3+0x^2+0x+8\\\\&-(x^3+2x^2)\\\\\\hline &-2x^2+0x+8\\\\&-(-2x^2-4x)\\\\\\hline &4x+8\\\\&-(4x+8)\\\\\\hline &0\\end{array}$$\n$$P(x)=(x+2)(x^2-2x+4).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 116
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-g11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^3-2x^2-5x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x+2)(x-3)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-2x^2-5x+6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1-2-5+6\\\\P(1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x-1$ is a factor. By long division,\n$$\\begin{array}{r|l}&x^2-x-6\\\\\\hline x-1&x^3-2x^2-5x+6\\\\&-(x^3-x^2)\\\\\\hline &-x^2-5x+6\\\\&-(-x^2+x)\\\\\\hline &-6x+6\\\\&-(-6x+6)\\\\\\hline &0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x^2-x-6)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x+2)(x-3).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 124
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-g11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^3-x^2-10x-8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+1)(x-4)(x+2)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-x^2-10x-8$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-1)&=-1-1+10-8\\\\P(-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x+1$ is a factor. By long division,\n$$\\begin{array}{r|l}&x^2-2x-8\\\\\\hline x+1&x^3-x^2-10x-8\\\\&-(x^3+x^2)\\\\\\hline &-2x^2-10x-8\\\\&-(-2x^2-2x)\\\\\\hline &-8x-8\\\\&-(-8x-8)\\\\\\hline &0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x^2-2x-8)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(x-4)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 124
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-g11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x^3+4x^2-3x-18$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+3)^2(x-2)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3+4x^2-3x-18$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(2)&=8+16-6-18\\\\P(2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x-2$ is a factor. By long division,\n$$\\begin{array}{r|l}&x^2+6x+9\\\\\\hline x-2&x^3+4x^2-3x-18\\\\&-(x^3-2x^2)\\\\\\hline &6x^2-3x-18\\\\&-(6x^2-12x)\\\\\\hline &9x-18\\\\&-(9x-18)\\\\\\hline &0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-2)(x^2+6x+9)\\\\P(x)&=(x+3)^2(x-2).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 124
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-g11-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x^3-19x-30$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-5)(x+2)(x+3)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-19x-30$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-2)&=-8+38-30\\\\P(-2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x+2$ is a factor. By long division,\n$$\\begin{array}{r|l}&x^2-2x-15\\\\\\hline x+2&x^3+0x^2-19x-30\\\\&-(x^3+2x^2)\\\\\\hline &-2x^2-19x-30\\\\&-(-2x^2-4x)\\\\\\hline &-15x-30\\\\&-(-15x-30)\\\\\\hline &0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+2)(x^2-2x-15)\\\\P(x)&=(x-5)(x+2)(x+3).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 124
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-g11-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$x^3-12x-16$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+2)^2(x-4)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-12x-16$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-2)&=-8+24-16\\\\P(-2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x+2$ is a factor. By long division,\n$$\\begin{array}{r|l}&x^2-2x-8\\\\\\hline x+2&x^3+0x^2-12x-16\\\\&-(x^3+2x^2)\\\\\\hline &-2x^2-12x-16\\\\&-(-2x^2-4x)\\\\\\hline &-8x-16\\\\&-(-8x-16)\\\\\\hline &0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+2)(x^2-2x-8)\\\\P(x)&=(x+2)^2(x-4).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 124
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-g11-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$x^3+4x^2-15x-18$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-3)(x+1)(x+6)$",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3+4x^2-15x-18$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-1)&=-1+4+15-18\\\\P(-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x+1$ is a factor. By long division,\n$$\\begin{array}{r|l}&x^2+3x-18\\\\\\hline x+1&x^3+4x^2-15x-18\\\\&-(x^3+x^2)\\\\\\hline &3x^2-15x-18\\\\&-(3x^2+3x)\\\\\\hline &-18x-18\\\\&-(-18x-18)\\\\\\hline &0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x^2+3x-18)\\\\P(x)&=(x-3)(x+1)(x+6).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 124
